[SPEAKER_00]: They drink a black liquid and then go into a dream state and hallucinate.

01:21:50.812 --> 01:22:02.857
[SPEAKER_00]: But what's worse is once they come out of this state, they become fiends, completely driven and consumed by hatred of all living things.

01:22:08.280 --> 01:22:23.925
[SPEAKER_00]: My brother-in-law tells me, which is interesting to me, that this alchemist, this assistant alchemist, may actually be able to find a cure for this sickness.

01:22:31.248 --> 01:22:32.068
[SPEAKER_00]: I will tell you truth.

01:22:34.608 --> 01:22:40.370
[SPEAKER_00]: My brother-in-law is quite possibly the most brilliant man that I have ever met.

01:22:42.731 --> 01:22:53.055
[SPEAKER_00]: He speaks of this gnome, Sibu Baron, with reverence and actually thinks him equal to his

01:22:58.395 --> 01:22:59.836
[SPEAKER_00]: What am I going to say?

01:22:59.936 --> 01:23:04.358
[SPEAKER_00]: His peer, Edium, the royal alchemist of Keoland.

01:23:06.499 --> 01:23:12.801
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, so to the GM, is Sibu Bear, is that the name of the assistant alchemist?

01:23:13.021 --> 01:23:13.322
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

01:23:14.582 --> 01:23:15.883
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

01:23:16.363 --> 01:23:17.183
[SPEAKER_01]: S-I-B-U?

01:23:18.264 --> 01:23:19.284
[SPEAKER_00]: S-E-E-B-O.

01:23:20.365 --> 01:23:22.045
[SPEAKER_01]: S-E-E-B-O Bear.

01:23:26.312 --> 01:23:32.477
[SPEAKER_01]: And... And what is his brother's name?

01:23:32.697 --> 01:23:34.679
[SPEAKER_01]: What is the, uh... Do you ask?

01:23:34.939 --> 01:23:35.199
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

01:23:36.060 --> 01:23:36.280
[SPEAKER_01]: Ugh.

01:23:38.182 --> 01:23:38.302
Ah.

01:23:38.542 --> 01:23:39.623
[SPEAKER_01]: Lord Jameson, what...

01:23:41.024 --> 01:23:43.746
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm going to need to know... a lot.

01:23:44.587 --> 01:23:46.929
[SPEAKER_01]: A lot more than you're used to telling me.

01:23:46.949 --> 01:23:49.091
[SPEAKER_01]: You said that we are engaged.

01:23:50.171 --> 01:23:51.232
[SPEAKER_01]: We're spies.

01:23:52.814 --> 01:23:54.535
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is something that I can do...

01:24:01.037 --> 01:24:08.621
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, unfortunately, I only just have tidbits of information myself.

01:24:08.661 --> 01:24:11.002
[SPEAKER_01]: However, I understand you do wish to know my brother-in-law's name.

01:24:29.770 --> 01:24:32.751
[SPEAKER_00]: I would expect you to go and meet with the crazed alchemist.

01:24:32.791 --> 01:24:35.352
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, I very much want you to do this.

01:24:35.932 --> 01:24:39.834
[SPEAKER_00]: There are many people I wish you to meet and gather information from in Monmurg.

01:24:40.614 --> 01:24:43.335
[SPEAKER_00]: My brother-in-law's name is Zafar.

01:24:46.937 --> 01:24:48.877
[SPEAKER_00]: Zafar Azein.

01:24:50.378 --> 01:24:55.980
[SPEAKER_01]: He is your wife's brother, therefore, soul, and you trust him.

01:24:56.867 --> 01:25:01.448
[SPEAKER_00]: I trust this man more than I trust anyone else in the world, besides my wife.

01:25:03.068 --> 01:25:03.589
[SPEAKER_01]: Zafar.

01:25:03.929 --> 01:25:05.409
[SPEAKER_01]: Z-A-F-A-R?

01:25:06.009 --> 01:25:13.771
[SPEAKER_00]: Z-A-R-F-A-R. No, Z-A-F-A-R. Z-A-F-A-R and last name again?

01:25:13.791 --> 01:25:15.151
[SPEAKER_00]: Azane.

01:25:15.271 --> 01:25:15.892
[SPEAKER_00]: A-Z-A-N-E.

01:25:21.353 --> 01:25:25.714
[SPEAKER_00]: The thing you should know about Zafar is he's a good friend

01:25:26.854 --> 01:25:34.378
[SPEAKER_00]: And courtier to the Duke of Gradsul and is very concerned with the Duke's activities.

01:25:36.019 --> 01:25:42.742
[SPEAKER_00]: Zafar is currently the head of transmutation in Gradsul.

01:25:46.023 --> 01:25:54.888
[SPEAKER_00]: He's also someone who used to act as head inquisitor for the Office of Forbidden Magic in Gradsul.

01:25:56.491 --> 01:26:13.144
[SPEAKER_00]: This man has held many offices and he knows the secrets of both the Duke of Gradsul, Lucian, and his father before him.

01:26:13.244 --> 01:26:21.350
[SPEAKER_00]: It is Zafar's suspicion that the Duke is being manipulated by the Toli.

01:26:22.773 --> 01:26:31.997
[SPEAKER_00]: and the Scarlet Brotherhood to bring about the destruction of the Monmurgian fleet for one purpose.

01:26:36.820 --> 01:26:45.284
[SPEAKER_00]: Our fleet has kept shipments from the Scarlet Peninsula to Monmurg at bay.

01:26:47.905 --> 01:26:51.827
[SPEAKER_00]: The Toli fleet is no match for ours, but

01:26:53.430 --> 01:27:06.375
[SPEAKER_00]: We have suspicions that the Scarlet Brotherhood are shipping arms, men, and other weapons of war into the Duchy of Berghof.

01:27:07.675 --> 01:27:10.796
[SPEAKER_00]: Our eyes are blinded and we cannot see this, however.

01:27:11.677 --> 01:27:20.680
[SPEAKER_00]: We cannot stop their ships, board them, and see what contraband they ship into the Duchy of Berghof.

01:27:25.229 --> 01:27:37.856
[SPEAKER_00]: I believe the purpose of this alliance between the Duke of Gradsul and Port Toli is to remove the princes of the Sea Principalities as an obstacle.

01:27:39.157 --> 01:27:47.561
[SPEAKER_00]: He's having help from the Plar of Westkeep and Toli Sagnon, the Prince of Port Toli.

01:27:49.782 --> 01:27:54.225
[SPEAKER_00]: All of the Suel are working together, conspiring in some way

01:27:57.359 --> 01:28:09.323
[SPEAKER_00]: To destroy the Sea Principalities and eliminate Monmurg and the Outer Isles as an impediment to whatever plans they have.

01:28:12.744 --> 01:28:21.087
[SPEAKER_00]: Zafar is actively involved in killing and ruining out and eliminating spies.

01:28:22.860 --> 01:28:48.690
[SPEAKER_00]: In the Magical Academy in Gradsul, he's doing this under some kind of a pretense that there are necromancers and traitors from Salinmoor, uncovered supposedly by Lord Phranck, but in truth he's looking for these agents of the Scholar Brotherhood.

01:28:59.128 --> 01:29:00.029
[SPEAKER_00]: You're not Suel.

01:29:02.491 --> 01:29:06.395
[SPEAKER_00]: And in truth, there are a few Oeridian mages that have your abilities.

01:29:09.678 --> 01:29:14.423
[SPEAKER_00]: I need someone that can look into magical things and find these out for me.

01:29:15.420 --> 01:29:31.784
[SPEAKER_00]: And also, I need someone that can root out spies in Monmurg and determine the truth of things.

01:29:37.465 --> 01:29:39.626
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, Monmurg must be intact.

01:29:39.746 --> 01:29:43.847
[SPEAKER_00]: You're very faint now, Steve.

01:29:44.307 --> 01:29:44.787
[SPEAKER_00]: Little better.

01:29:46.625 --> 01:29:50.186
[SPEAKER_00]: It's almost like you have a wire that gets pulled out a little bit or something.

01:29:50.886 --> 01:29:51.746
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, it might be.

01:29:52.467 --> 01:29:56.968
[SPEAKER_01]: Kind of lame.

01:29:57.568 --> 01:29:58.908
[SPEAKER_01]: Maybe I'll just get a different headset.

01:30:01.829 --> 01:30:02.890
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

01:30:03.330 --> 01:30:04.470
[SPEAKER_01]: What would you have me start?

01:30:04.510 --> 01:30:14.913
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, if I go to Salmore or if I go to Houle and I search, I still would like to try to move.

01:30:17.770 --> 01:30:19.070
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, truthfully

01:30:46.238 --> 01:30:50.641
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, I fear your small nation of Idee is already lost.

01:30:52.822 --> 01:31:08.873
[SPEAKER_00]: By the summer months, it will be overrun, like I said, not by the Southern Province, but by the forces of the Scarlet Brotherhood, who, by the way, will not stop there, but will actually overrun the Southern Province itself.

01:31:09.854 --> 01:31:10.614
[SPEAKER_00]: If Hazar is...

01:31:11.513 --> 01:31:13.494
[SPEAKER_00]: All my service to you and the Sea Princess.

01:31:50.909 --> 01:31:55.832
[SPEAKER_00]: It is possible for me to get a message to him, yes, even though he may not recognize it.

01:31:57.813 --> 01:32:02.015
[SPEAKER_01]: I have taken Karmor's battle flag.

01:32:03.436 --> 01:32:08.859
[SPEAKER_01]: Perhaps that could be the bona fides that might get his attention.

01:32:11.481 --> 01:32:17.524
[SPEAKER_01]: I would surrender that flag to you gladly if it would help your message be delivered.

01:32:17.904 --> 01:32:19.065
[SPEAKER_00]: Is Phyla with him?

01:32:21.348 --> 01:32:22.809
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, Philo is with me.

01:32:23.229 --> 01:32:27.692
[SPEAKER_00]: Then perhaps what I'll do is send the message to Philo, as he knows me.

01:32:30.333 --> 01:32:34.156
[SPEAKER_00]: And he can counsel this on Loth, one way or the other.

01:32:35.817 --> 01:32:40.500
[SPEAKER_00]: However, the seas between here and there are not safe anymore, and...

01:32:43.221 --> 01:32:46.123
[SPEAKER_01]: If you but try, then...

01:32:51.862 --> 01:33:01.668
[SPEAKER_01]: I understand.

01:33:02.429 --> 01:33:08.993
[SPEAKER_00]: So, where I would like you to start, Jude, go to the Alchemist, as you've suggested.

01:33:09.213 --> 01:33:09.954
[SPEAKER_00]: Please start there.

01:33:10.874 --> 01:33:15.077
[SPEAKER_00]: However, there is another person that I would like you to go and talk to as well.

01:33:15.737 --> 01:33:17.779
[SPEAKER_00]: Two other people, in truth.

01:33:20.964 --> 01:33:35.308
[SPEAKER_00]: One is a spy that Lord Phranck had insinuated into Monmurg several months ago.

01:33:37.049 --> 01:33:46.672
[SPEAKER_00]: An elf who goes by the name of Calise, who actually has worked with some of my men in the past.

01:33:49.720 --> 01:34:01.187
[SPEAKER_00]: She was able to identify a traitor that was working for the Toli and bring him to my attention.

01:34:02.248 --> 01:34:05.750
[SPEAKER_00]: I had an inkling about it, but she was able to prove the fact to me.

01:34:05.770 --> 01:34:09.413
[SPEAKER_01]: Was he also Scarlet Brotherhood?

01:34:09.793 --> 01:34:10.273
[SPEAKER_01]: What's that?

01:34:10.834 --> 01:34:12.375
[SPEAKER_01]: Was he also Scarlet Brotherhood?

01:34:12.695 --> 01:34:16.998
[SPEAKER_00]: No, he was just, he was actually one of my main...

01:34:20.060 --> 01:34:20.981
[SPEAKER_00]: Harbormasters.

01:34:22.221 --> 01:34:24.283
[SPEAKER_00]: Someone I relied on heavily.

01:34:24.423 --> 01:34:33.749
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm afraid that he passed to the Toli the patrols of both my squadron and the admirals of the Outer Islands.

01:34:36.130 --> 01:34:38.352
[SPEAKER_00]: I think he was just paid for.

01:34:40.954 --> 01:34:47.558
[SPEAKER_00]: I sent him to Gradsul, actually, so that Zafar could take a look at him, and he determined that was the case.

01:34:49.252 --> 01:34:54.514
[SPEAKER_00]: When he returned, I thought it useful to be able to put him in Lord Phranck's hands.

01:34:55.254 --> 01:35:10.561
[SPEAKER_00]: So I had Gouge and Karmirg capture him, with the help of Khaleesi, and deliver him to a pirate, one of the pirates, in Port Torvin.

01:35:11.661 --> 01:35:13.722
[SPEAKER_00]: Now this is where things become strange.

01:35:16.474 --> 01:35:28.180
[SPEAKER_00]: Because even though I had made this deal with Lord Phranck, I believe the pirate that destroyed Torvin was working for Lord Phranck.

01:35:34.267 --> 01:35:35.487
[SPEAKER_00]: So when you talk to...

01:35:35.507 --> 01:35:43.589
[SPEAKER_01]: This is a save Lord Phranck that was seeking to discover a cure perhaps for the black sickness?

01:35:43.769 --> 01:35:44.229
[SPEAKER_00]: Correct.

01:35:45.150 --> 01:35:52.431
[SPEAKER_00]: So the truth is I have no idea where this Lord Phranck's loyalties lie.

01:35:55.532 --> 01:35:57.933
[SPEAKER_01]: You're a good judge of character though.

01:35:58.433 --> 01:36:02.194
[SPEAKER_01]: So this being that he had something

01:36:06.005 --> 01:36:10.888
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, he's very convincing, but Jude, this is what I would say about the man.

01:36:12.930 --> 01:36:14.751
[SPEAKER_00]: And Zafar backs this up.

01:36:16.112 --> 01:36:17.293
[SPEAKER_00]: He's very ambitious.

01:36:20.776 --> 01:36:21.336
[SPEAKER_00]: Very...

01:36:26.440 --> 01:36:27.520
[SPEAKER_00]: Very ambitious.

01:36:28.521 --> 01:36:30.943
[SPEAKER_00]: And his loyalty seemed to lie with himself.

01:36:35.678 --> 01:36:52.221
[SPEAKER_00]: Zafar has talked to me and said we need to have a way to exploit Phranck and make him spy on our side because he's very close to this Cebu character that I've told you about.

01:36:52.921 --> 01:37:02.923
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's the one thing Zafar seems very interested in is making Cebu an agent of ours.

01:37:08.018 --> 01:37:13.105
[SPEAKER_00]: The way through Cebu, Zafar says, is through Lord Phranck.

01:37:14.227 --> 01:37:24.562
[SPEAKER_00]: Because Lord Phranck, as powerful an evoker as he is, can act foolishly sometimes.

01:37:33.247 --> 01:37:45.933
[SPEAKER_00]: And then the third man is a merchant who actually worked in Salonmar for many years smuggling goods from Monmurg into the city of Saltmarsh.

01:37:49.335 --> 01:37:57.519
[SPEAKER_00]: He had dealings with Lord Phranck and has some insight into what's going on in Saltmarsh itself.

01:38:01.424 --> 01:38:08.406
[SPEAKER_00]: I would like you to speak to him to get a feeling for Lord Phranck and the other people in the area.

01:38:08.606 --> 01:38:15.448
[SPEAKER_00]: And also to get a little bit of perspective on what had been going on in Saltmarsh before then.

01:38:15.808 --> 01:38:21.950
[SPEAKER_00]: Because apparently... Phranck, Cebu...

01:38:23.113 --> 01:38:39.828
[SPEAKER_00]: And the man who has been appointed the plar in the area were sent originally to Salonmore to investigate a group or cult called the Sons of Olad.

01:38:40.889 --> 01:38:43.511
[SPEAKER_00]: And I believe this merchant may know something of it.

01:38:46.914 --> 01:38:49.356
[SPEAKER_01]: Is the merchant presently in Monmurg?

01:38:50.725 --> 01:38:52.007
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the funny thing.

01:38:52.127 --> 01:39:07.062
[SPEAKER_00]: The merchant was actually a Monmurgian merchant who is actually quite a rich man, but ran his smuggling business out of salt marsh.

01:39:07.603 --> 01:39:10.746
[SPEAKER_00]: You see, Keoland and Monmurg are

01:39:12.467 --> 01:39:15.309
[SPEAKER_00]: Very much into taxes on one another.

01:39:16.069 --> 01:39:21.293
[SPEAKER_00]: And goods that come from Monmurg were taxed at nearly 25%.

01:39:21.673 --> 01:39:24.375
[SPEAKER_00]: And vice versa.

01:39:25.656 --> 01:39:28.878
[SPEAKER_00]: But this merchant had a way of...

01:39:29.926 --> 01:39:35.528
[SPEAKER_00]: Getting past that by selling his goods in Salamore as if they came from other places.

01:39:36.428 --> 01:39:44.410
[SPEAKER_00]: Everybody seemed to turn a blind eye, but the Duke of Gradsul, however, sent Lord Phranck down there to stop the practice.

01:39:47.231 --> 01:39:53.353
[SPEAKER_00]: This merchant was arrested by Lord Phranck in the Plar and questioned extensively, however...

01:39:56.868 --> 01:40:05.272
[SPEAKER_00]: Lord Phranck seemed to extort a pair of ships from him and let him go for 5,000 gold coins.

01:40:12.975 --> 01:40:15.396
[SPEAKER_01]: So let me just summarize.

01:40:17.016 --> 01:40:18.377
[SPEAKER_01]: Lord Phranck is seeking...

01:40:38.969 --> 01:40:50.791
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes, he spent time there and I think he will give you a measure of who Lord Phranck really is.

01:40:50.931 --> 01:40:52.051
[SPEAKER_01]: The merchant?

01:40:52.131 --> 01:40:52.791
[SPEAKER_01]: Or Lord Phranck?

01:41:12.466 --> 01:41:22.330
[SPEAKER_00]: The Merchant is an Oeridian mix with actually men from the West, so no, definitely as far from Suel as you can be.

01:41:23.831 --> 01:41:26.892
[SPEAKER_00]: Friendly chap, actually, and quite bright.

01:41:27.553 --> 01:41:28.473
[SPEAKER_00]: I like his company.

01:41:29.934 --> 01:41:37.617
[SPEAKER_00]: Lord Phranck is definitely Suel, although he's from no great house, and from what I understand, not really a lord, but a...

01:41:38.569 --> 01:41:43.575
[SPEAKER_00]: How do you best see me operating within the confines of Monmurg and the employee?

01:42:11.116 --> 01:42:15.919
[SPEAKER_01]: It's true, the city is becoming dangerous.

01:42:15.939 --> 01:42:16.740
[SPEAKER_01]: What I would suggest is this.

01:42:16.760 --> 01:42:22.403
[SPEAKER_01]: You take up residence in the old slum that you used to be in.

01:42:38.309 --> 01:42:39.150
[SPEAKER_01]: Ferds, yes.

01:42:39.950 --> 01:42:41.491
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes, Ferds.

01:42:42.172 --> 01:42:44.634
[SPEAKER_00]: Gouge and Karma are coming in and out of there.

01:42:45.374 --> 01:42:46.916
[SPEAKER_00]: You can meet with them if you want.

01:42:47.356 --> 01:42:49.998
[SPEAKER_00]: I would say pick up your old lifestyle, as it were.

01:42:51.339 --> 01:43:01.507
[SPEAKER_01]: I will need at least, when I talk to the elf, please.

01:43:03.048 --> 01:43:06.971
[SPEAKER_01]: Does she need to know?

01:43:10.845 --> 01:43:11.065
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

01:43:13.287 --> 01:43:14.748
[SPEAKER_00]: She will guess it.

01:43:15.768 --> 01:43:20.432
[SPEAKER_00]: She's not unsmart about these things.

01:43:20.512 --> 01:43:25.516
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, I have a feeling she will know exactly what you are up to in many ways.

01:43:26.617 --> 01:43:33.602
[SPEAKER_00]: However, through her, it is possible for you to get an audience with Lord Phranck at some point.

01:43:37.363 --> 01:43:42.704
[SPEAKER_01]: Is Lord Fonk in Salamore or the Salt Marsh?

01:43:42.924 --> 01:43:44.585
[SPEAKER_01]: Or is he in Monmurg still?

01:43:44.645 --> 01:43:45.685
[SPEAKER_01]: He's not in Monmurg.

01:43:45.965 --> 01:43:46.946
[SPEAKER_00]: No, no, no, no.

01:43:47.026 --> 01:43:54.067
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, what's strange is when he left Monmurg two months ago, he was actually captured by the Toli.

01:43:55.868 --> 01:44:01.589
[SPEAKER_00]: And they took him to the fortress in the middle of the bay.

01:44:01.609 --> 01:44:04.050
[SPEAKER_00]: I think you sailed past it.

01:44:06.598 --> 01:44:08.340
[SPEAKER_00]: On your way with Owen Black.

01:44:09.521 --> 01:44:15.386
[SPEAKER_00]: He was captured and kept there, and from what I understand, he managed to escape one night.

01:44:18.449 --> 01:44:21.552
[SPEAKER_00]: He's a very resourceful man, it appears.

01:44:24.394 --> 01:44:29.719
[SPEAKER_01]: I came from the D with some thousand blue pieces.

01:44:40.183 --> 01:44:43.264
[SPEAKER_00]: There's no lack of gold, Jude.

01:44:44.005 --> 01:44:47.486
[SPEAKER_00]: You tell me what you need as far as bribes go, and you'll get the money.

01:44:50.047 --> 01:44:54.629
[SPEAKER_00]: However, if you're looking for food, you'll be on your own for that.

01:44:56.970 --> 01:44:59.251
[SPEAKER_01]: Maybe I should take those bottles of wine?

01:45:00.271 --> 01:45:05.814
[SPEAKER_00]: I would keep that, definitely, for yourself, and not sell them, but drink them down.

01:45:07.294 --> 01:45:09.435
[SPEAKER_01]: I would still much like to keep them.

01:45:11.996 --> 01:45:28.795
[SPEAKER_00]: I would appreciate it to be sure, but in truth, as I said, of course you'll not go hungry if you're working with me, but unfortunately the fare will be porridge and rice more than anything else.

01:45:41.702 --> 01:45:43.383
[SPEAKER_00]: I can understand you need the fare.

01:45:47.785 --> 01:45:48.185
[SPEAKER_01]: Alright.

01:45:49.626 --> 01:45:52.087
[SPEAKER_01]: Who is your man that I should talk to without bothering you?

01:45:54.808 --> 01:45:57.769
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll have someone contact you at Ferds.

01:45:59.310 --> 01:45:59.730
[SPEAKER_01]: Very well.

01:46:01.311 --> 01:46:08.214
[SPEAKER_00]: And in fact, in truth, I will have Khaleesi contact you.

01:46:09.715 --> 01:46:10.155
[SPEAKER_00]: Khalees.

01:46:13.536 --> 01:46:15.316
[SPEAKER_01]: Then I wouldn't recognize her.

01:46:15.416 --> 01:46:15.696
[SPEAKER_01]: How?

01:46:17.097 --> 01:46:17.737
[SPEAKER_00]: She's an elf.

01:46:18.657 --> 01:46:19.297
[SPEAKER_00]: You'll know her.

01:46:24.098 --> 01:46:24.538
Very well.

01:46:25.559 --> 01:46:26.059
[SPEAKER_01]: Not many.

01:46:26.359 --> 01:46:34.981
[SPEAKER_00]: Get a measure of her and I'll let her know that you're an old agent of mine and that she's acting as a cutout for me.

01:46:36.201 --> 01:46:37.121
[SPEAKER_01]: Very well.

01:46:37.161 --> 01:46:40.762
